      "text": "John had his raiment of camel’s hair, Matt. 3:4. than meat, and the body than raiment, Matt. 6:25 (Luke 12:23; 3 Ne. 13:25). why take ye thought for raiment, Matt. 6:28 (3 Ne. 13:28). man clothed in soft raiment, Matt. 11:8 (Luke 7:25). transfigured … his raiment was white as the light, Matt. 17:2. put his own raiment on him, Matt. 27:31. his raiment became shining, exceeding white, Mark 9:3. his raiment was white and glistering, Luke 9:29. they parted his raiment, and cast lots, Luke 23:34. kept the raiment of them that slew him, Acts 22:20. having food and raiment let us be therewith content, 1 Tim. 6:8. a poor man in vile raiment, James 2:2. same shall be clothed in white raiment, Rev. 3:5. white raiment, that thou mayest be clothed, Rev. 3:18.",
